// A map of Lanternroot's overworld (ADR-0061): its ground through the legend, one row a string, and the things on it.
// Coordinates are [column, row], counted from 0 at the top left. Lanternroot is 80 x 56 tiles, the town overhaul
// (Concept/v0.3/09), seven districts round the Lantern Square: Home Hollow in the south-west (the start at (13, 45),
// facing down, out of the door of home), Waterside with the pond and its one bridge and the forge, the Lantern Square
// with the Lantern Root and the shut Hall, Warm Hearth Row to the east on Main Street, the Archive Quarter and Fern's
// Grove to the west, the North Green and the Old Stones, and the Root Gate Road with the drill yard in the east and
// south-east. The lamp lane runs north from the square to Lumen's shrine; its six lamps are group "lane", dark until
// lesson 3. Solid bands of trees hold the edges. Only the cabbage plot and the Old Stones are fenced, each with a
// two-tile gate; every opening of the square and the Root Gate mouth has gate pieces that stay walkable.
// Flat things (the footbridge) are anchored a row above where they lie and sunk, so walkers draw over them.
// Things that take code (TownThings, ADR-0061) are props with an id and a program: the cabbage-plot gate and the
// crossroads signpost. Each one's file is in things/, with its hints and starter code.
// v0.4 added the music box by the Warm Hearth (it opens the music box), Pell's map table (the map), a small farm by the
// cabbage plot, a pine and a rock: props that give items to the bag are listed in pickups.jsonc.
